MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Bread and the Eagles feel like natural next choices because I have been choosing familiar older songs and best-of collections; Bread also fits the softer, nostalgic mood I enjoy with Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie.",
    "Bob Seger's hits connect with my interest in classic rock collections, while Partners appeals to the vocal duet interest reflected in Cheek to Cheek, though it is a lower priority today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Adele and Imagine Dragons do not fit my current desire for older familiar hits, even though I have occasionally chosen contemporary pop such as Born This Way.",
    "Traveller does not match what I want on this visit because I am not seeking a country album, and Greatest Hits: Decade #1 gives me too little indication of whose music I would be choosing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My occasional interest in contemporary pop seems to have been taken as a stronger guide than my repeated choices of older music collections.",
    "A greatest-hits title alone seems to count too much; I still need to recognize the artist or songs and want that particular sound."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The repeated appeal of melodic, nostalgic songs matters more to me right now than a broad connection to pop or rock.",
    "Something can suit my taste without being an immediate choice: I would choose Bread, the Eagles, and Bob Seger before Partners or Earth Wind & Fire today."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in older hits but gave too much weight to occasional contemporary listening and too little to my current nostalgic mood."
}
